## Reviewer Report

**Scope of this diff**: v2.32.0 → v2.32.1 patch release. Core change: `dispatch-author.sh`'s final emptiness check (`tr | sed | grep -q` under `set -o pipefail` → `grep -q`'s early-exit-on-match SIGPIPEs the upstream `tr`/`sed`, and pipefail then reports the *pipeline* as failed even though content was found, misclassifying successful runs as `empty_output`) fixed by swapping `grep -q` for `grep -c ... > /dev/null` (drains stdin, no early exit, same 0/1 exit semantics). Plus a regression test, release-hygiene mirrors/version bumps, and three payload-mirror catch-ups.

I traced the pipeline-status mechanics by hand against `scripts/dispatch-author.sh:48` (`set -uo pipefail`) and the codex/grok/cc-shim/agy branches (`scripts/dispatch-author.sh:136-219`): all four runner branches funnel through the single shared post-processing block at `scripts/dispatch-author.sh:215-223`, so the fix and its regression test (which exercises the `codex` branch via a stub `--bin`) cover all four dispatch families, not just one.

### 🟡 Minor (recommended)

- `docs/BACKLOG.md:97-101` — The `✅ DONE (2026-07-05, v2.31.17)` entry attributes the `empty_output` misclassification to a "late-flush"/"detached child or very late buffered write" theory and claims it was `RESOLVED v2.31.17` via the content-quiescence wait. This diff's own `CHANGELOG.md` (new v2.32.1 section, "CORRECTION" paragraph) explicitly states that narrative **was a misdiagnosis** — the real cause was the pipefail+`grep -q` bug fixed here, and the marker-aware quiescence redesign it spawned was reverted pre-merge. `docs/BACKLOG.md` is not touched anywhere in this diff, so it now contains a stale, contradicted-by-the-same-release causal claim marked "DONE." Consequence: a future debugging session (or an agent skimming `docs/BACKLOG.md` per `CLAUDE.md`'s "Where context lives" table) can re-chase the refuted theory — which is exactly the failure this release's own CHANGELOG says already happened once. Fix: append a superseded-note to the BACKLOG entry pointing at the v2.32.1 CHANGELOG correction (one line, e.g. `SUPERSEDED 2026-07-05 (v2.32.1): "late-flush" diagnosis above was wrong; root cause was pipefail+grep -q — see CHANGELOG v2.32.1`).

- `docs/metrics/surface-lines.json:2-3` (UNVERIFIED, live-fact) — `prose` moves 10759→10865 (+106 lines, +0.99%) but no hunk in this diff adds/removes lines under `skills/` or `references/` (the field's own counting formula, per its `note`, is `find skills references -name *.md -type f | sort -u | xargs cat | wc -l`). The three mirror-catchup hunks discussed below are single-line *replacements* (same line count before/after), so they can't account for the delta either. I have no Bash tool in this review to run `git diff v2.32.0..HEAD -- skills references | wc -l` or the counting formula directly against the working tree, so per the Fact-driven live-system-fact rule I mark this **UNVERIFIED** rather than asserting a defect — it's plausible the full v2.32.0→HEAD commit range (which the CHANGELOG says involved "concurrent-session divergence") includes skills/references edits not present in the diff I was handed. Below the 5%-growth threshold that would mandate a CHANGELOG `prose-justification:` line, so it isn't independently gated either way. Fix direction: before merge, re-run the formula against the actual working tree and confirm 10865 (this is literally what `preflight-release.sh --update-baseline` is supposed to guarantee — flag is that I can't corroborate it from the artifacts alone).

