### ✅ Verified Clean

- `scripts/dispatch-author.sh:215-223` — Core fix traced by hand against bash `pipefail` semantics (`set -uo pipefail` at `scripts/dispatch-author.sh:48`): `grep -q` exits at first match without draining stdin → upstream `sed`/`tr` SIGPIPE (exit 141) → under pipefail bash reports the rightmost *non-zero* PIPESTATUS entry, which becomes 141 even though `grep -q` itself returned 0 (match found) → `if !` inverts a real match into "empty." `grep -c '[^[:space:]]' > /dev/null` must read to EOF to produce an accurate count, so it never triggers the early-close/SIGPIPE path, while preserving identical 0/1 exit-status semantics to `grep -q`. Confirmed this is the *only* `grep -q` in a piped (not direct-on-file) position in the file (searched full file, no other occurrence missed).
- `scripts/dispatch-review.sh:255,505-508` — Confirmed all `grep -q` calls here take a file argument directly (`grep -qF "$NONCE" "$DIFF_FILE"`, `grep -q '...' "$BLOCK_FILE"`), never piped through an upstream process — immune to the SIGPIPE class, corroborating the CHANGELOG's claim that dispatch-review was never affected.
- `hooks/tests/dispatch-output-quiescence.test.sh:126-135` — New regression test genuinely exercises the fixed code path: stub emits `head -c 6000 /dev/urandom | base64` (~8KB), dispatched via `--runner codex --bin <stub>` (direct-file RAW_LOG capture per `scripts/dispatch-author.sh:143-147`, so the SIGPIPE risk is isolated to the post-capture emptiness-check pipeline being tested), asserts `exit 0` / `status:authored` / bounded elapsed time. All helper functions used (`assert_le`, `assert_ge` local to the file; `assert_eq`, `assert_contains`, `fail`, `finalize_test`, `TEST_TMP`, `REPO_ROOT` from `hooks/tests/lib.sh`) verified to exist and behave as called. Confirmed `hooks/tests/run.sh:77` globs `*.test.sh` automatically — no manual registration needed.
- `platforms/codex/plugin/scripts/dispatch-author.sh:215,219` — Byte-identical to the canonical fix; confirmed via `sync-codex-plugin-skills.sh`'s whole-`scripts/`-directory copy contract.
- `scripts/lib/output-quiescence.sh` and all four `wait_output_quiescent` call sites — confirmed untouched by this diff (grep across repo), consistent with the CHANGELOG's claim that the earlier quiescence-lib work is unaffected/unchanged by this fix.
- Version/release-hygiene mirrors — `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`, root `plugin.json`, `platforms/codex/.agents/plugins/marketplace.json`, `platforms/codex/plugin/.codex-plugin/plugin.json`, `README.md`, `README.zh-TW.md` all consistently bumped 2.32.0→2.32.1; semver classification (PATCH — bug fix, no new skill/agent) correct per `CLAUDE.md`'s versioning table. `docs/projects/INDEX.md` new row and `docs/projects/ongoing-maintenance/2026-07.md` new row both well-formed and consistent with existing table conventions.
- No test suite was executed for this review — this task provides only Read/Grep/Glob (no Bash), so `hooks/tests/run.sh` (L1+L2) could not be run. Correctness was assessed by static trace of bash pipeline/pipefail semantics and manual code reading only; this bound is disclosed here per the "No silent caps" rule rather than silently assumed passing.
- Reviewed full diff for scope creep — every changed line traces to the task except the three mirror-catchup hunks noted above (flagged as Suggestion, not Major, since verified functionally inert).

